    "reason": "[ev-09d5e26554e5] says that running in `--datapath-mode=lb-only` for plain Docker mode \"now requires\" adding `--enable-k8s=false`, and that without it Kubernetes is assumed to be present. That makes the subject the `--enable-k8s` cli-flag. The change fits now-required: a flag that was previously optional must now be set to `false`, so after=\"false\" is copied literally from the text. The requirement only applies in lb-only plain-Docker setups, which is a matter for the applicability aspect. That aspect is not under review here.",
